;; FH-ROOT-002 — hot reload keeps the root's identity, and does not reseed.
;;
;; A declared view is a descriptor VALUE, so a hot reload mints a NEW
;; descriptor object for the redefined view. But the value it carries holds
;; the same qualified `:view-id`, and the root's identity — its `:root-id` —
;; is derived from that id, so the reload's root-id is unchanged. The
;; body/generation churn is an internal fact of the descriptor object,
;; never part of the identity.
;;
;; So re-mounting the same root into the same container is idempotent: it
;; RE-RENDERS the existing host root instead of allocating a second one. A
;; second host root on one container is a React error and would tear the
;; whole tree down and reseed it; reusing the live one is what makes the
;; reload preserve identity. This is the donor's known-hard case — the
;; hot-reload matrix's frame-non-reseed / body-advance cells — recast for
;; the interpreted root: same identity, new body, host root preserved.
;;
;; The reload is SIMULATED by two descriptors that share one view-id and
;; differ only in their body — exactly how a redefinition presents (the
;; same qualified identity, a fresh body generation), and how the donor's
;; `register-view-generation!` models a reload without redefining a var.
{:fh/id "FH-ROOT-002"
 :fh/law
 "A root's occurrence identity is its derived root-id — the mounted view's qualified id, which a redefinition does not move — so re-mounting the same root into the same container re-renders the existing host root, and the reloaded body renders without reseeding the host root."

 :root-id :re-frame.freehand.root-hmr/app

 ;; the two body generations of the reloaded view — same view-id, different text
 :before "before"
 :after  "after"

 ;; the reload re-renders the EXISTING host root (identity preserved, no reseed)
 :same-host-root true

 ;; non-vacuity control: a mount into a DIFFERENT container is a genuinely
 ;; new root, so its host root is NOT the reloaded one — the reuse above is
 ;; a real decision, not an always-true tautology.
 :fresh-container-host-root :distinct}
